// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64 || host-linux-arm64
// RUN: not %gopp build -emit=gir %S/Inputs/iface-refused.gopp 2>&1 | FileCheck --implicit-check-not=error[E %s
// P04.06: what the lowering of methods and interfaces leaves to a later task
// is refused with one E0439 that names it, where it is: a method value and
// a method expression (P04.07, closures), an `@Virtual` method and a child
// type in an interface (P04.22, once, where the child is made), an operator
// method (P04.23), a method of a generic type (P04.08) and a method on a map
// type (P04.18: its receiver goes by a hidden pointer to the caller's map,
// PAR-1, PAR-10); a method marked `@Extern("C")` is no C function (E0442).
// The other side: `Sq.Area` as a plain method with `Shape` is fine (the
// iface run tests run it), and nothing else in this file draws an error.
// CHECK: :5:1: error[E0439]: a method with @Virtual, @Abstract or @Override (P04.22) is not supported
// CHECK: :12:1: error[E0439]: an operator method (P04.23) is not supported
// CHECK: :16:1: error[E0439]: a method on a map type (P04.18) is not supported
// CHECK: :20:1: error[E0439]: a method of a generic type (P04.08) is not supported
// CHECK: :38:1: error[E0442]: invalid @Extern on Ext: a method cannot be a C function
// CHECK: :29:7: error[E0439]: a function value (P04.07) is not supported
// CHECK: :30:7: error[E0439]: a function value (P04.07) is not supported
// CHECK: :48:6: error[E0439]: a type that extends another (P04.22) is not supported
